WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.372
Most beginner NumPy problems come from a small set of recurring issues.

00:00:04.372 --> 00:00:06.512
The first is wrong shape.

00:00:06.512 --> 00:00:13.092
Before combining arrays, print the shapes and confirm that the dimensions match your intended operation.

00:00:13.092 --> 00:00:15.562
The second is wrong axis.

00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:20.372
Ask whether you want one result per row or one result per column.

00:00:20.372 --> 00:00:23.377
Another issue is unexpected dtype.

00:00:23.377 --> 00:00:26.702
If values behave strangely, inspect the data type.

00:00:26.702 --> 00:00:30.607
Broadcasting errors usually mean the shapes are not compatible.

00:00:30.607 --> 00:00:33.382
Compare both shapes rather than guessing.

00:00:33.382 --> 00:00:40.987
If a summary returns nan, check whether missing values are present and whether a nan-aware function is

00:00:40.987 --> 00:00:45.077
appropriate. Finally, remember the difference between views and copies.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:48.332
A slice may share memory with the original array.

00:00:48.332 --> 00:00:55.942
A strong debugging routine is simple: print the shape, print the dtype, inspect a small sample of values,

00:00:55.942 --> 00:00:59.686
and verify the axis before rewriting large sections of code.
